craze's Messages API driver
===========================

This package, and its Fantasy adapter in the package above it
(internal/harness/llm/messages_adapter.go), take their design from
Fantasy's Anthropic language model:

    https://github.com/charmbracelet/fantasy
    charm.land/fantasy v0.43.2
    providers/anthropic/anthropic.go and providers/anthropic/error.go

-- the mapping of a conversation's messages to Messages API content blocks
(toPrompt), of a stream's events to Fantasy stream parts (Stream), and of
the API's errors to retryable and final failures (toProviderErr). The code
here is craze's own, written against the standard library rather than the
Anthropic SDK, and it differs where craze needs it to (plan 044 §3.2-§3.3):
thinking is always adaptive, summarized, and bound with drop_block behind
its beta; caching is the system block's breakpoint and the top-level
automatic one; a thinking block's signature fragments are joined and
replayed byte for byte; usage is overwritten only by the counts each event
reports; a tool call is reported at its own block's stop; any break in the
stream's protocol is an incomplete stream; and the account's model list is
read here too.

